# Before writing or changing music, read music/README.md (style, moods, format).
# Built after the title song (music/title.scrim). The waltz kept, but in D minor: a clarinet opens
# on the toy tune (D E F A G), an accordion on the off-beats, a music box picking high.
title    Town
composer Claude
about    Smoke from the chimneys and the well in the square, the one memory that never fades, but darker now: a waltz in D minor, a clarinet opening on the toy tune (D E F, A G, F), an accordion on the off-beats, a music box picking high, glass harmonica chords and a low fretless bass; the glass bird calls at the phrase ends. The town has no enemies, so it only knows explore and treasure.
tempo    92
beats    3
steps    4
reverb   0.45

# moods (music/README.md)
# mood explore:  lead accordion ost pad bass bird
# mood treasure: ost pad bird wonder

voice lead     clarinet   vol=0.62 pan=-0.1 rev=0.4
voice accordion accordion  vol=0.24 pan=0.3  center=D4 gate=0.6
voice ost      musicbox   vol=0.3  pan=0.45 rev=0.6
voice pad      glassharp  vol=0.2  pan=-0.25 center=A3 att=0.4 rel=0.8
voice bass     fretless   vol=0.7  glide=0.08
voice bird     crystal    vol=0.5  pan=0.4  rev=0.7
voice wonder   crystal    vol=0.28 pan=-0.35 rev=0.6

# Dm Dm Bb Bb Gm Gm A A
pattern A
lead    | D5----- E5- F5--- | A5------- G5--- | F5----------- | .----------- |
lead    | D5----- E5- F5--- | Bb5------- A5--- | G5----- F5- E5--- | A4------- .--- |
bird    | _ | _ | _ | A6 D6+E6---------- |
bird    | _ | _ | _ | .------- E6 A5+B5-- |
